      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T16:57:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t this still wrong? The `ss[INDEX_TOTAL_PSS]` includes shmem that is mapped to userspace, since it\u0027s read from `/proc/$pid/smaps[_rollup]`, and the pss value reported there includes shmem: https://cs.android.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/fs/proc/task_mmu.c;l\u003d677-684\n\nSo even with this change aren\u0027t we oversubtracting shmem?\n\nFurthermore, I don\u0027t think `getCachedSizeKb()` entirely includes shmem, since we do subtract `Mapped` from `/proc/meminfo`: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/com/android/internal/util/MemInfoReader.java;l\u003d104?q\u003dgetCachedSizeKb\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain\n\nwhich includes both file backed mapped pages, and shmem mapped pages.\n\nI think we might want to re-write this as:\n\n```\nlostRAM \u003d memInfo.getTotalSizeKb() - meminfo.getAnonPagesKb() - memInfo.getFreeSizeKb() - memInfo.getKreclaimable() - NR_FILE_PAGES -\nmemInfo.getSlabUnreclaimable() - memInfo.getVmallocUsed - memInfo.getPageTablesKb() \n```\n\n`NR_FILE_PAGES` can be read from the `nr_file_pages` entry in `/proc/vmstat` and includes the file LRU pages (both active and inactive), buffer head pages, swapcache pages, all shmem pages (including ones allocated by kernel drivers), mapped and unmapped file pages.",
